---
import { site } from '../data/profile';

---

<section id="roots" class="roots" aria-labelledby="roots-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="roots-grid">
      <aside class="roots-left" aria-label="Identity">
        <div class="roots-symbol" aria-hidden="true">M<span>.</span></div>

        <div class="roots-identities">
          <div class="identity"><span class="identity-dot"></span>Tamil-Canadian</div>
          <div class="identity"><span class="identity-dot"></span>Scarborough → Markham → Pickering</div>
          <div class="identity"><span class="identity-dot"></span>Tamil · English · French</div>
          <div class="identity"><span class="identity-dot"></span>Anime &amp; Japanese culture</div>
          <div class="identity"><span class="identity-dot"></span>DJ · after hours</div>
          <div class="identity"><span class="identity-dot"></span>Elden Ring · Wukong</div>
          <div class="identity"><span class="identity-dot"></span>Lifeguard &amp; aquatics leader</div>
          <div class="identity"><span class="identity-dot"></span>Competitor at heart</div>
        </div>

        <div class="symbol-row">
          <div class="symbol-item">
            <span class="sym" lang="ja">月</span>
            <span class="sym-label">mathee<br />= moon</span>
          </div>
          <div class="symbol-item">
            <span class="sym" lang="ja">龍</span>
            <span class="sym-label">year of<br />the dragon</span>
          </div>
          <div class="symbol-item">
            <span class="sym" lang="ja">波</span>
            <span class="sym-label">varuna<br />waves</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="roots-coord mono">{site.coords}<br />{site.location.toLowerCase()}</p>
      </aside>

      <div class="roots-right">
        <p class="section-label">// roots</p>
        <h2 id="roots-title" class="section-title">One person, <em>several places.</em></h2>

        <div class="roots-bio">
          <p>
            I was born in Toronto, grew up in <strong>Scarborough</strong>, was raised in
            <strong>Markham</strong> — one of Canada’s most multicultural cities — and now live in
            <strong>Pickering</strong>. The son of Tamil parents from Sri Lanka. My first language was
            Tamil. I picked up English, then French through school. I grew up surrounded by Japanese
            anime, Chinese New Year, and every cuisine you can imagine. That breadth shaped how I think.
          </p>
          <p>
            My name, <em>Matheesan</em>, means moon in Tamil — <em>mathee</em> (<span class="tamil" lang="ta">மதி</span>). I’ve always felt a pull
            toward water: lifeguard at 16, aquatics programs, awards through the Life Saving Society. My son
            was born in the year of the dragon and named after Varuna — the Hindu lord of storms and waves.
            The symbols chose us as much as we chose them.
          </p>
          <p>
            Music and games are the other two languages. I DJ — basshall and dancehall, South
            Indian, R&amp;B, gaming OSTs, whatever the room needs — and I keep a rotation of <em>Elden Ring</em>, <em>Wukong</em>, <em>Mario Kart</em>,
            <em>Valorant</em> and <em>Overwatch</em>. Both are about pattern, timing and losing gracefully
            until the next attempt.
          </p>
          <p>
            Engineering became the arena: complex problems, no obvious answers, no ceiling on how good you
            can get. My final-year ML project — Twitter data into interaction graphs into community structure
            — was the first time a model found something I hadn’t. Later I was putting LLM agents
            in front of real callers and learning that the interesting part is not the demo. It’s the gap
            between <strong>“the tests are green”</strong> and <strong>“it works on a real call.”</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            These days I’m at <strong>WayTrade</strong>, building the marketplace layer for biofuels,
            feedstocks and critical materials. Small team, physical trade, one record for the
            commercial, operational and compliance work — the kind of system where a delayed
            railcar shows up in inventory, production, cash and paperwork at the same time.
          </p>
          <p>
            I’m genuinely optimistic about AI, and specific about it. I’m a software engineer first — the
            tooling is a multiplier, not a substitute for the craft. The work I care about is not replacing
            judgment; it’s making judgment legible, testable, and safe enough to automate.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .roots {
    padding: 4.5rem 0 5rem;
    background: var(--bg2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    scroll-margin-top: 6rem;
  }

  .roots-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.78fr 1.5fr;
    gap: 5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .roots-left { position: sticky; top: 7rem; }

  .roots-symbol {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 8rem;
    line-height: 0.8;
    color: var(--wave1);
    margin-bottom: 2.2rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .roots-symbol span { color: var(--gold); }

  .roots-identities {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .identity {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--text2);
  }

  .identity-dot {
    width: 4px;
    height: 4px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .symbol-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.8rem;
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
    padding-top: 1.8rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .symbol-item { text-align: center; }

  .symbol-item .sym {
    font-family: var(--jp);
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    color: var(--gold);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .symbol-item .sym-label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text3);
  }

  .roots-coord {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--text3);
  }

  .roots-right .section-label { margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
  .roots-right .section-title { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.4vw, 3.4rem); margin-bottom: 1.8rem; }

  .roots-bio p {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--text2);
    margin-bottom: 1.3rem;
  }

  .roots-bio p:first-child { color: var(--text1); }

  .roots-bio strong { font-weight: 500; color: var(--moon); }
  .roots-bio em { font-style: italic; color: var(--moon2); }
  .roots-bio .tamil { font-family: var(--tamil); font-style: normal; font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--moon2); }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .roots { padding: 3.4rem 0 4rem; }
    .roots-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; }
    .roots-left { position: static; }
    .roots-symbol { font-size: 5.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
    .roots-identities { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .roots-coord { display: none; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .roots-identities { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .symbol-row { gap: 1.2rem; }
    .roots-bio p { font-size: 1.08rem; }
  }
</style>
